## Dependency pinning (supply chain)

- **Next.js** and `@next/eslint-plugin-next` are pinned in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` `catalog:` (currently 16.2.6).
- Apps use `"next": "catalog:"` — no floating `^` on framework packages.
- Bump Next: edit catalog version → `pnpm install` → review `pnpm-lock.yaml` → run `pnpm ops:validate:local`.
- CI uses `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` — lockfile must be committed.
- Root `minimumReleaseAge` (48h) applies to new publishes — do not bypass with ignore env vars.
- Do **not** add `postinstall` scripts that shell out to npm for `update-browserslist-db` or `baseline-browser-mapping`.

## Desktop boundaries

- UI calls `lib/command-client.ts` only — never `invoke()` in components.
- `apps/desktop-backend` has no product UI — Rust/commands only.
- Remove dead code (e.g. legacy `components/case-workspace.tsx` in U11) when replacing flows.
